<title>USA: Comerica unit issues $200 mln in 10-yr debt.</title>
<headline>Comerica unit issues $200 mln in 10-yr debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Comerica Bank was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p>Comerica Bank is the lead bank of Comerica Inc, a bank holding company with subsidiaries in Michigan, California, Texas and Florida. It reported assets of $34 billion at September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to fund growth, Comerica said.</p>
<p>BORROWER COMERICA BANK</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.25 PCT   MATURITY 6/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SUB NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.716  FIRST PAY DATE 12/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 7.29 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD 64 BPS     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
</text>
